  "notes": [
    "Instances of eval/spec/attributes.md for SMB (ADR-0020 section 1); replaces docs/plans/smb-map-coverage.md.",
    "match: a claim belongs to the line when every word of one group appears in the claim's name (words are lowercased, camelCase and punctuation split, plural s dropped; xpos becomes x pos). exclude: words that take a claim off the line. Matching is vocabulary, not the answer.",
    "ref: the reference symbols that grade the line (scripts/score-mapping.mjs). span: how many bytes from the symbol's address count as the same thing, when the reference gives no size (BCD digit runs). A run never sees this file: trio.sh voids a blind run whose shell reads eval/, hacks/ or mappings/.",
    "Lines with grader claude are judged from the run's saved images; the scorer lists them as needs-judge.",
    "v3 (2026-10-09, before the first sheet-5 run): the coin and timer routine lines exclude helper vocabulary and the digit-helper line takes it, so a claim about SMB's shared BCD adder (DigitsMathRoutine, called by GiveOneCoin and RunGameTimer) is graded on the helper's line. Vocabulary only; no reference changed.",
    "v4 (2026-10-09, eval/runs/20261009-1414-sheet5b-entry-dispatch-palette): E3.vram_writer added (attributes.md E3 lists the renderer's writers); E1.nmi excludes writer vocabulary, since a claim about the NMI's VRAM writer had landed on the NMI line.",
    "v5 (2026-10-09, before the first sheet-2 run): B2.metatiles also takes '? block' / 'block tiles' names, B3.player_sprites 'Mario tiles' / 'sprite layout'. Vocabulary only.",
    "v6 (2026-10-09, eval/runs/20261009-1428-sheet2-text-tiles): B4.game_text accepts every labelled string of the GameText table (GameTextOffsets indexes them from GameText); v5 accepted only the first, whose gap-span ends where WorldLivesDisplay, the WORLD card's text, begins.",
    "v7 (2026-10-09, before the first sheet-4 run): pointer-table lines take 'level address/table' and 'enemy table/offset' names. Vocabulary only.",
    "v8 (2026-10-09, eval/runs/20261009-1729-sheet4-level-data): D2.area_pointers excludes 'enemy', so an 'area enemy data pointer table' claim is graded on the enemy line.",
    "v9 (2026-10-09, eval/runs/20261009-1749-sheet3-engine-input-enemies): the enemy slot lines span 6 bytes, SMB's six enemy slots (Enemy_X_Position $87 to Fireball_X_Position $8D, Enemy_State $1E to Fireball_State $24 in the source); v8 read the equates as single bytes and graded right 6-slot array claims disagrees."
  ],
